# ============================================================
# WISHMail — Postmaster environment (v0.5.2)
# ============================================================
#
# This file is committed and `.env` is not (`.gitignore`: `.env*` with
# `!.env.example` negated back in).
#
# A value is BLANK where it is yours to supply — every secret, every location,
# every id. Two carry a SAFE DEFAULT instead, because there is one worth having
# and it is not a secret: HEDERA_NETWORK=testnet, which is the only network this
# version deploys on (§15.5), and MCP_BIND=127.0.0.1, which is loopback because
# a resource server holding 402 state (§14.2, D-109) should not be reachable off
# the host until someone decides otherwise.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# THE RULE (Sonic, 2026-09-08)
#
#   `.env` holds secrets, the network selector, and runtime locations.
#   It never holds a copy of a value whose home is somewhere else.
#
# Four tiers, and each fact lives in exactly one of them:
#
#   .env                        secrets · which network · where things run
#   app/src/ops/networks.ts     per-network constants, keyed by HEDERA_NETWORK
#                               (mirror URL, USDC asset, facilitator and fee
#                               payer, rate source, fee caps — each with its
#                               citation)
#   spec/pins.json              §18.4's set: the standards pins, and the stamp
#                               token and treasury per network (§4.1)
#   app/deployment/<net>.json   every other fact about one deployment — the
#                               accounts, the topics, each entity's creation
#                               transaction and consensus timestamp
#
# So there are NO entity IDs here. The token id is read from `spec/pins.json`
# (§4.1) and everything else from the ops record for the selected network. A
# second copy in `.env` is a second source of truth, and the one that goes
# stale is always the copy.
#
# P-13 and CLAUDE.md §3: no private-key material in any committed file, in
# `spec/pins.json`, in the ops record, in a commit message, or in a log line.
# Nothing in this project prints a key. Where each private key was generated
# and where it lives is recorded per role in `app/OPERATIONS.md` — the
# location, never the material.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Which network
# `hedera:mainnet` is defined and undeployed at this version (§15.5); selecting
# it stops the run rather than half-provisioning it.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
HEDERA_NETWORK=testnet

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Operator / payer (D-140)
# Pays every network fee (§3.5, §4.6, D-47); `payTo` for the money leg of a
# purchase (§14.2); momentary bearer of the first-contact stamp (§4.4); holds
# the price topic's submit and admin keys (D-142).
#
# The account id is here rather than in the ops record because it is an input
# to provisioning, not a product of it — it is the one account this deployment
# did not create (D-140: reused).
#
# *_DER_KEY is a DER-encoded ED25519 private key, the form `PrivateKey.fromStringDer`
# reads. Only `app/src/ops/identity.ts` ever sees these values.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
POSTMASTER_PAYER_ID=
POSTMASTER_PAYER_DER_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Treasury (D-140)
# Holds the unissued $POSTAGE supply (§4.1) and its supply key (D-148);
# receives affixed postage (§4.3), doorbell fees (§4.4), and the return-receipt
# fee inside postage (§14.1). This key is HOT: §14.2's purchase is atomic, so
# it signs the stamp leg of every buy_stamp. The split from the operator is
# containment and accounting, not cold custody.
#
# Generated in-process at provisioning and appended here by identity.ts.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
TREASURY_DER_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Postmaster-agent (D-140)
# The service's own Correspondent identity — an operational choice, not a spec
# role (§1.4 gives POSTMASTER no doorbell and no profile obligation).
#
# NO POSTMASTER SERVICE CODE PATH READS THIS. The namespace exists so that
# T-P13-1's check is structural rather than a matter of intention:
#   npm run p13:check
# Generated in-process at provisioning and appended here by identity.ts.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
AGENT_DER_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime locations
#
# WISHMAIL_STATE_DIR is the durable record §14.2 requires of the resource
# server. D-109 fixes that the MCP server holds the 402 state and accepts only
# requirements it issued, which makes it stateful across the 402 and the retry
# — and T-P11-5 and T-P11-6 test that the state survives a restart: a replayed
# payload returns the original StampReceipt with no second transfer, and
# requirements issued before a restart are accepted after it. In-memory state
# fails both. Nothing in it is a secret; it is not this file's contents, only
# where they are kept.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
WISHMAIL_STATE_DIR=
MCP_BIND=127.0.0.1
MCP_PORT=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional
# Defaults to the selected network's mirror URL in app/src/ops/networks.ts.
# Override only to point at a different mirror node; a mirror node is a read
# interface and never a broker (P-3, P-4).
# ------------------------------------------------------------
MIRROR_NODE_URL=
